  "scope_notes": [
    "SmHCR receives a borrowed source and owns a transformed working scene. Visible curves return to source coordinates; owned NURBS snapshots cross a mutex-protected C ABI with RAII cleanup.",
    "Parallel Direction is normalized and points toward the eye. Application input uses the current camera independently of the CPlane. Perspective without an explicit parallel Direction declines and retains source picks.",
    "The approximation request is split equally between HCR tracing and curve conversion. The command uses document absolute tolerance and a 0.05-radian tracing angle. These settings and sampled tests are not a continuous error certificate.",
    "Tests cover box reversal/scaling/depth/source preservation, axial and oblique sphere equators, both torus circles, rational outer/hole trims from both sides, open surfaces, manifold mesh input, invalid inputs, staging failure with Redo preservation, source picking and one Undo/Redo entry.",
    "InternalEdges enables visible features, smooth edges and seams per source object. Native recipes verify additional oblique-box edges. Full Rhino InternalEdges semantics and mutual visibility between separate source objects are unqualified.",
    "Meshes use their actual physical triangulation, including warped quads. InternalEdges may expose triangulation edges. Non-manifold imports can decline. Admission limits apply after native computation and do not bound runtime.",
    "Seven closed Python recipes dispatch to public RhinoCommon Silhouette.Compute and the native Rust command. Raw definitions, samples, lengths and ordering are retained for future audit. SDK visibility, direction, parameterization and segmentation parity are pending.",
    "No new licensed Rhino launch or capture was performed. The previously recorded Wine SSPI startup failure remains unresolved; docs/oracle-sspi.md describes the independent public loader diagnostics."
  ],
